  "reason": "Evidence: RNA dominates (0.485-0.591 vs 0.208 for image), and the best config so far is rna_only/multiprofile/pca_n2000/avgpool at 0.591. Multiprofile+avgpool clearly outperforms singleprofile and transformer aggregation. Question: Can a more expressive RNA encoder (scgpt, a pretrained single-cell foundation model) improve on PCA's linear projection while keeping the proven multiprofile+avgpool pipeline? This isolates the encoder effect with all other settings held at their best-known values. Why this is the best use of experiment 5: It directly tests whether the current 0.591 ceiling is due to PCA's limitations or is a fundamental limit of the RNA-only pipeline, which determines whether to invest remaining budget in better encoders or pivot to multimodal fusion. With 5 experiments left, establishing the RNA encoder ceiling before adding fusion complexity is the most informative next step."
